  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Fiat became part of the Baud family’s food-retail enterprise through his marriage to Geneviève Baud, a descendant of Franprix’s founder. He served as a senior executive of Leader Price and participated in holding structures connected with Franprix and Leader Price before the businesses passed into the Casino group. That grocery platform supplied the main commercial foundation of his wealth.\n\nA polar-capable research vessel became Fiat’s main vehicle for exploration and environmental science. He conceived it around the principles of adventure, science and education. Its laboratories, diving systems and other equipment were made available to researchers and Monaco’s oceanographic initiatives, supporting fieldwork in remote waters. The first major programme included Arctic testing before a three-year scientific expedition.",
